            "review_title": "Review at Ngoc Luc Bao Restaurant",
            "review_text": "cgully1\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan11 contributions\n1\nSuper weird experience\nOct 2018 • Couples\nMy husband and I decided to go to this restaurant after a nice day out in Halong Bay. We were greeted warmly by the front door staff and escorted to the 5th floor restaurant. What an amazing view! It kind of ends there though...we are given one menu to share by an awkward waitress who stood at our table while we flipped through like 10 pages of items. As she handed us the menu she asked what we wanted. My husband said \"Time to read the menu.\" Of course she didn't understand (I don't fault her for that) but she was very persistent. Finally we ordered a drink to get her to leave so we could actually read the menu in peace. (The drinks never came...she didn't understand.) We had just had a large seafood lunch and were interested in chicken or beef for supper...there were many chicken and beef options on the menu. We then decided on what we wanted and got the waitress' attention. She came back and we proceeded to order grilled chicken, bread, rice and vegetables. The grilled chicken was priced at 550 000 dong which is abnormally high for Vietnam (even in classy restaurants). Even with pointing at the menu, the girl didnt understand what we wanted. She then went and got a girl from another table to come over. She comes over and says \"can you help me?\" (Obviously meaning \"can I help you?\") We proceed to order and she says \"no! No bread! You cannot!\" Uhh Why not? Finally she says they didnt have bread...(hmm its on the menu multiple times but ok). Then we order the grilled chicken. She says again \"no you cannot! Only seafood!\" We said \"but its on your menu...?\" She said \"no you not order chicken. Only seafood!\" At this point my husband and I were really weirded out by the whole creepy place. We decided to leave without any food and find a different restaurant. Did I mention that a small meal for two would have cost like $85 USD? The building was beautiful but the wait staff have zero serving/customer service skills. All in all I wouldnt waste your time here unless you want expensive seafood and aggressive service from staff. If you do, knock yourself out. (We have heard Vietnamese restaurant standards are different than other countries. It's definitely true. We've been here almost 3 weeks now so we've had good service, bad service and everything in between. This place was next level bad...what a weird, creepy place!)\nRead more\nWritten October 27, 2018",
