            "review_title": "Review at Ngoc Luc Bao Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Nadia G\nMilton, Canada27 contributions\n1\nHighway Robbery\nOct 2017 • Couples\nDo not. I repeat do not go here. If I can give 0 star I would. They totally ripped us off. We got 2 spring rolls, 1 lobster that hardly had any meat in it and 2 beers for $300 cnd / 4Million dong. The manager is fake friendly and wouldn't give us a chance to look at the menu, its almost like he knew we would change our minds if we had time to process the prices. He brought the owner and chef to meet us lol, made it such a big event & insisted to take pictures of us even though we didn't want that. There was no privacy and 0 professionalism. The manager is dishonest. What a rip off. These people have no idea how to price & 0 ability to communicate properly and clearly with tourists. If you really want to eat at a fancy place like this, ask for the price before you order anything. I have never seen prices like this. We eat at fancy places back home but this was over the top highway robbery. I am 100% sure they have different menus for tourists and different ones for locals. Do not go in there blind sighted. As soon as we got our bill the manager and owner disappeared lol! What a joke. These people are dishonest and scam artists and not to be trusted. They took advantage of our kindness & do not deserve to have their restaurant open. It's a big show , that's what it is. A big show to take your money. Horrible place.\nRead more\nWritten October 15, 2017",
